Load decks of sp_mes1 against ngspice-45, written by ../load.py mes1.
Builds on PATH: ngspice-45 jfngv2gd3zvi5cmr9vrqfhnziipqd09n (source hfvpfb0bgw9819wkb7kzpdaasbd0hd5r, devices/mes),
VACASK dhxz6l3iac3r2b8n91kcz04a0j3hs4s6 (devices/spice/mes1.va, ngspice-47-159 vadng-pre-48).
Run: `nix develop .#testing -c tests/fixtures/families/load_run.sh mes1`. i(vd) in A, |i(vd)| at 1 GHz for acg/acd.
nom is 27 C, m=1, the control of off (80 C, m=3); both give area=2. Regions (vgs, vds) in ../load.py.
The oracle of the AC readings (fd.py, last lines): each nominal region's operating point moved 1e-5 V on the gate
(base) and the drain (collector), whose central differences are gm and gds of the DC law, against |i(vd)| at 1 kHz.
It holds where the conductance is well above the capacitive current at 1 kHz and the differences' resolution (ngspice
prints 12 digits: about 5e-11 S): not in cutoff, whose 1 kHz reading is the capacitances'.
The model has no temperature law on either side (off is nom times m to 1e-12). ngspice-45 lists no `m` in the
MESFET parameter table (devices/mes/mes.c) and still multiplies by it, as VACASK's $mfactor does.
Result: no difference. DC to 4.2e-5 (a cutoff pA), AC to 3e-13, both AC the derivatives of the DC law (1e-7).

